# TypeScript — Common Components (Warn)

Apply when touching files under `src/components/common/**`. Type **new or modified** exports only.

## Required

| Rule | Rationale |
|------|-----------|
| **Props named `ComponentNameProps`** | Prefer `NPSelectProps` over `PropsType` (existing inconsistency in `NPOTPField`, `LoanSelectionScreen`). |
| **No `any` in new props** | Use unions, generics, or `unknown` with guards. |
| **Typed callbacks** | `(value: string) => void` instead of `Function`; MUI/React events use proper types (`SelectChangeEvent`, `ChangeEvent<HTMLInputElement>`). |
| **Extend shared form types** | Common inputs extend `NPInputType` via `interface XProps extends NPInputType` rather than duplicating fields. |
| **Discriminated unions for variants** | Multi-mode components use `type Step = "select" \| "loading"` (see `DiyVerificationScreenView.tsx`). |

## Example

```typescript
import { SelectChangeEvent } from "@mui/material";

export interface NPSelectProps {
  label: string;
  value: string;
  options: { code: string; label: string }[];
  onChange: (event: SelectChangeEvent<string>) => void;
  disabled?: boolean;
}

export const NPSelect = ({ label, value, options, onChange, disabled }: NPSelectProps) => { ... };
```

## Legacy touch-only paths

When fixing an unrelated bug, do not refactor the entire component to replace existing `Function` or `any` props.
